-- title:
--   Finiteness of the Hecke algebra over ℤ
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a natural number with $N \neq 0$, let $k$ be an integer, and let $S$ be an arbitrary set of natural numbers. Consider the space $S_k(\Gamma_0(N))$ of cusp forms of weight $k$ for the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_0(N)$ and its ring of $\mathbb{C}$-linear endomorphisms. Inside that ring, [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N k S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) is the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra generated by the set of operators consisting of the linear Hecke operators `heckeTLin k hℓ hℓN` attached to primes $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$, together with the operators `heckeULin k hqN` attached to primes $q$ with $q \mid N$ and $q \notin S$. The theorem asserts that this subalgebra is a finite $\mathbb{Z}$-module, i.e. finitely generated as an abelian group. No positivity or parity hypothesis is imposed on the weight $k$, and the elements of $S$ are not required to be prime; $S$ merely excludes generators from the generating set.
--
--   This is the integral finiteness of the anaemic Hecke algebra of weight $k$ and level $N$ away from $S$, the basic structural input that makes Hecke eigenvalues algebraic integers and allows localisation of the Hecke algebra at maximal ideals. It is used in the project by the statements producing deformation-theoretic and local data from the Hecke algebra, such as the existence of characteristic-zero algebra homomorphisms into discrete valuation rings and the $U_q$-relations at ramified primes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_moduleFinite_heckeAlgebra.lean

